# Rule Routing

Before acting, check which rules apply to the current task:

- **All tasks**: Follow `model-harness.mdc` (no external side-effects unless explicitly requested)
- **All tasks**: Follow `coding-guidelines.mdc` (simplicity, surgical changes, explicit assumptions)
- **Shell commands**: Execute via tmux session as defined in `tmux-shell-execution.mdc`
- **Git commits**: Use identity from `git-identity.mdc` and message format from `git-rules.mdc`
- **Python code** (OpenStack): Follow `openstack-code-style.mdc` — run `tox -epep8` after changes
- **OpenStack repos**: Read the project `AGENTS.md` at the repo root for project-specific conventions

When creating or deleting a rule in `.cursor/rules/`, update this routing list to keep it in sync.
